import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout title="band repos — Band Docs">
  <h1>band repos</h1>

  <p>
    The <code>band repos</code> command group manages the repos registered with Band. A
    repo is a directory on your filesystem — typically a Git repository — that you've
    registered with Band so it can create worktrees inside it.
  </p>

  <h2>List repos</h2>

  <p>Display all registered repos.</p>

  <pre><code>band repos list</code></pre>

  <p>Example output:</p>

  <pre><code>NAME        PATH                         WORKTREES
my-app      /Users/dev/repos/my-app   3 worktrees
api-server  /Users/dev/repos/api      1 worktree
docs-site   /Users/dev/repos/docs     0 worktrees</code></pre>

  <h2>Add a repo</h2>

  <p>
    Register a directory as a Band repo. The path must point to an existing Git repository.
    The repo name is derived from the directory name unless you pass <code>--label</code>.
  </p>

  <pre><code>band repos add /Users/dev/repos/my-app
band repos add . --label "Frontend"</code></pre>

  <p>
    Band reads <code>.band/config.json</code> from the repo directory if it exists. If the
    config file is missing, the repo is still registered and you can add the file later.
  </p>

  <h2>Remove a repo</h2>

  <p>
    Unregister a repo <strong>by name</strong>. This does not delete the directory on disk —
    it only removes the repo (and any tracked worktrees) from Band's database.
  </p>

  <pre><code>band repos remove my-app</code></pre>

  <h2>JSON output</h2>

  <p>All subcommands support <code>--output json</code> for machine-readable output.</p>

  <pre><code>band repos list --output json</code></pre>

  <p>Example JSON output:</p>

  <pre><code set:html={`{
  "repos": [
    {
      "name": "my-app",
      "path": "/Users/dev/repos/my-app",
      "worktreeCount": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "api-server",
      "path": "/Users/dev/repos/api",
      "worktreeCount": 1
    }
  ]
}`}></code></pre>

  <h2>Notes</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Repo names default to the basename of the directory; pass <code>--label</code> to override.</li>
    <li>Repo names must be unique. Adding a directory whose name conflicts with an existing repo will fail.</li>
    <li>Repos are stored in Band's local SQLite database (<code>~/.band/band.db</code>).</li>
    <li>The repo directory should be a Git repository for worktree features (worktrees, diff, branch status) to work.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
